{
  "tema": 8916,
  "slug": "hay-ahi-ay",
  "titulo": "Hay, ahí and ay",
  "subtitulo": "«Ahí hay un perro. ¡Ay, qué miedo!»",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Three words that sound alike: hay (there is / there are, from haber), ahí (there, the place) and ¡ay! (oh! / ouch!). Hay and ay sound the same; ahí has two syllables, stressed on the í.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Word",
            "What it is",
            "Sounds like",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "**hay**",
              "verb (haber)",
              "_eye_ (one syllable)",
              "_there is / there are_"
            ],
            [
              "**ahí**",
              "adverb of place",
              "_a-EE_ (two syllables)",
              "_there_ (near you)"
            ],
            [
              "**¡ay!**",
              "interjection",
              "_eye_ (one syllable)",
              "_oh! ouch! oh no!_"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Hay** says something **exists**: **Hay olas** (_There are waves_). It never changes for plural."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Ahí** points to a **place**: **Ponlo ahí** (_Put it there_). The accent on the **í** splits it into two syllables."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**¡Ay!** expresses pain, surprise or worry, usually between **¡ !**: **¡Ay, me duele!** Mexicans love **¡Ay, no!** and **¡Ay, qué bonito!**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "English _there_ has two jobs that Spanish splits: _**There** is a café_ = **Hay** un café; _The café is over **there**_ = El café está **ahí**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Hay== muchas olas hoy.",
              "en": "There are a lot of waves today."
            },
            {
              "es": "Deja las llaves ==ahí==, en la mesa.",
              "en": "Leave the keys there, on the table."
            },
            {
              "es": "==¡Ay!== Me pegué en el dedo.",
              "en": "Ouch! I hit my toe."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Ahí== ==hay== una taquería muy buena.",
              "en": "There's a really good taco place over there."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Hay== tortillas? —Sí, ==ahí== están.",
              "en": "Are there any tortillas? —Yes, there they are."
            },
            {
              "es": "==¡Ay, no!== Se me olvidó el kimono.",
              "en": "Oh no! I forgot my gi."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==hay== nadie en la playa.",
              "en": "There's nobody on the beach."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Ahí== nos vemos.",
              "en": "See you there. / See you around."
            }
          ]
        }
